279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T18:45:40Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T18:45:40Z","body":"Added an Engine::is_editor_hint() condition for setting the icon name.\r\n\r\nEffectively what setting an icon name does, is if you have an icon theme that overrides the godot icon then even if compiled locally the icon from the icon theme will be used instead of the default godot icon (ie no `.desktop` entry requirede). With an icon named `godot.png` in my `~/.local/share/icons/` I managed to get a different icon for godot which is not the one we provided.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20250605_193137](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5288634e-5b86-4e9e-93de-774201727d41)\r\n\r\nThe change is that now running games will not get godot's icon override.\r\n\r\nThe only people not having an icon name could affect are app developers who somehow have an icon theme for their own app which they prefer over the actual icon of the app which won't be applied when running locally. Users will hopefully have `.desktop` entries if they're getting to the point of theming icons an